-- ====================================================================
-- Migration 0045: seed realistic PILOT students for hands-on testing
-- of the daily dashboard across all 7 weekdays.
--
-- Per-course student counts are hand-picked (not a flat 10-per-course)
-- to stay within each real instructor's actual weekly capacity from
-- src/data/schedule.js: an instructor teaching N courses across their
-- D real teaching day(s) can see at most 10 solo students per day (10
-- x 30 min = 5 hours, 16:00-21:00), so 10 x every course would wildly
-- overflow a single day for instructors who teach several courses
-- (e.g. خلیل دلاوران: 5 courses, only یکشنبه/پنج‌شنبه). Courses are
-- weighted per the school's real mix described by the owner: guitar
-- is the busiest course, solfege/theory/rhythm are light (1-3
-- students). Each course's students are split round-robin across
-- their instructor's real day(s) so no single day ever exceeds 10.
--
-- 22 solo courses -> one class per student (one-on-one, per the
-- school's real model). 1 group course (آموزش موسیقی کودک) -> one
-- class shared by its 10 students, one 60-minute session.
--
-- Sessions are inserted directly (not via the materializer) for the
-- 7-day window 2026-09-15 (today, Tue) .. 2026-09-21 (Mon) -- one
-- full pass over all 7 Persian weekdays. Matching class_schedules
-- rows are also created (effective_from/to limited to this same
-- window) so the daily dashboard's own materializer recognizes these
-- classes without duplicating today's already-inserted sessions.
--
-- PILOT marker: students.notes / classes.notes contain 'PILOT DATA'
-- and national_code is prefixed 'PILOT' -- NOT 'TEST DATA' / '99', so
-- migration 0043's cleanup logic does not touch this dataset. Remove
-- later via a dedicated migration once real students are entered.
--
-- Financial mix (rotates across students, 5 patterns): fully paid,
-- partially paid, overdue & unpaid, pending & not yet due, open
-- invoice with a partial payment against it.
--
-- Attendance mix (rotates across students, 7 patterns): all present
-- so far, one absence, one excused absence, an all-future pending
-- week, a present/absent mix, a mid-week withdrawal, one pending
-- makeup request.
-- ====================================================================


